Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:44:32 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] target/riscv: Add Spacemit X100 CPU type

Adds a CPU definition for the X100 cores present in the Spacemit K3 SoC.
The CPU definition is based on information from datasheet[1] and Linux
device tree. The custom CSRs are based on what the Spacemit K3 bootrom,
U-Boot SPL and OpenSBI write to during the boot process.

[1] https://github.com/spacemit-com/docs-chip/tree/main/en/key_stone/k3

Signed-off-by: Anirudh Srinivasan <asrinivasan@oss.tenstorrent.com>

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://lore.kernel.org/qemu-riscv/20261124-spacemit_k3-v1-1-e911d6e88542@oss.tenstorrent.com/]

[tgamblin: taken from the v2 work in progress at
 https://github.com/asrinivasanTT/qemu/commit/8388c5f3226b8ee350cd4c8bc9993f1c7f66fa35]
Signed-off-by: Trevor Gamblin <tgamblin@baylibre.com>
